    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Kline-Life-Sports-Learning-Complex/Assistant-Softball-Coach_JR100588": {
      "title": "Assistant Softball Coach",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Athletics - Softball Position Details Position Summary The Assistant Coach supports the Head Coach in all aspects of an athletic program, including but not limited to player development, the recruitment of prospective student-athletes, administration of practices, game preparation and execution, and program operations. This role assists with the planning and implementation of training sessions, provides feedback and mentorship to student-athletes, and helps develop strategies for competition. Assistant Coaches may also be responsible for specific areas such as scouting, video analysis, strength and conditioning, or skill development for particular positions or groups. Additional responsibilities often include supporting the academic progress and personal development of student-athletes, coordinating team travel and logistics, assisting with fundraising and community service initiatives, and contributing to the overall culture and success of the program. The position requires strong communication, leadership, and organizational skills, as well as a commitment to sportsmanship, inclusion, and the academic mission of the institution. Assistant Coaches are expected to work collaboratively with the Head Coach, athletic department staff, and other campus partners, and to model professionalism and integrity in all interactions. Essential Functions: Oversee the management and mentoring of the softball team, and specifically the pitching staff, by fostering a culture of accountability, discipline, and a strong team mentality. Assist with the strength and conditioning program for the softball team. Reinforce the head coach's expectations for player behavior, commitment, and standards of performance both on and off the field. Help players develop their mental and mechanical skills while cultivating a positive, competitive team environment. Play a pivotal role in recruiting talented softball student athletes to the program through scouting, evaluation, and communication with prospective student-athletes and their families. Manage the recruiting database (e.g., Front Rush/Slate) and clearly communicate the values and culture of the college and the softball program during the recruiting process. Establish a strong pipeline of future student-athletes who align with the program's mission. Assist the head coach in planning and coordinating daily team practices, ensuring that training sessions are purposeful and focused on developing both individual skills and team strategy. Must be able to throw batting practice and hit fungos. Contribute to game days through the scouting of opponents, and provide input into game plans and lineup decisions. Help analyze game film, create video analysis, and offer coaching feedback to improve team performance. Coordinate all travel logistics for the softball team, including organizing transportation, accommodations, and meal planning for away games and tournaments. Support the team’s fundraising efforts and facilitate team events that promote community engagement and program growth. Assist with marketing and promotional activities, including managing communication with alumni, recruits, and the broader softball community through social media, emails, and other. Coordinate with grounds grew to assist in field game prep. Other Duties and Responsibilities Other duties as determined and assigned. Supervisory Responsibilities Not responsible for supervising others. Requirements: Bachelor's degree required. Master's degree preferred. This position is subject to the Pennsylvania Act 153 Clearance consisting of the Pennsylvania Criminal History Record Information Check, Pennsylvania Child Abuse Certification, and Federal Criminal History Record Information Check pursuant to Pennsylvania law and Dickinson College policy. Valid driver's license for the operation of a company owned, rented or leased vehicle. Minimum Work Experience 1-3 years Independence of Action Work progress is monitored by supervisor/manager; incumbent follows precedents and procedures, and may set priorities and organizes work within general guidelines established by supervisor/manager. Physical/Environmental Demands Outdoor environment: Employees work outdoors and may not be protected from weather conditions. Noise: There is sufficient noise to cause you to shout in order to be heard above noise level. EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Carlisle-Pennsylvania/Communications-Officer_JR100583": {
      "title": "Communications Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Public Safety Position Details Dispatcher To support campus law enforcement and other public safety functions by performing activities related to processing service requests and questions; which include communications and dispatch, status monitoring, information development and communication, and records and file maintenance in a computer-aided environment. The Communications Center serves as the primary link between the public and DPS Police Officers in the field. The Communications Center is the central coordinating agency for emergency telephone calls and requests for assistance. After hours the Communications Center serves as the main information, responsible for aiding the college community and its guests with requests for service and general inquiries. Essential Functions Handles emergency and non-emergency telephone calls, prioritizes calls, and channels pertinent information to officer and supervisory personnel. Makes necessary emergency notifications. Monitors and operates police and other radio systems, fire and intrusion alarm systems, and security camera systems, and dispatches officers and other emergency personnel as needed. Monitors computer terminals for messages directed to the Department, information related to local criminal activity, and officer safety messages. Confirms warrants with responsible agencies. Provides the public with assistance on complaints and informational services, lost and found property, bicycle registration, directions, and other services. Uses tact and discretion. Observes strict confidentiality rules. Directs persons to proper supervisory level as necessary. Accurately documents officer status, location and activity. Preserves accurate logs of incoming service requests and action taken and enters, updates, and recovers information from a Computer Aided Dispatch (CAD) system. Preserves and updates various logs and records of activities, such as radio transmissions, telephone calls, tow requests, and equipment failure logs. Demonstrates knowledge of police terminology and procedures, Pennsylvania criminal and civil law as it pertains to police communications, campus geography, police services, and College policies and procedures pertaining to police communications. Provides assistance and information to persons registering vehicles at Public Safety and issues parking decals. Performs various tasks to ensure proper operation of equipment such as setting and resetting computer system, video display terminals, and printers. Assists with College fleet reservations and issues keys for reserved fleet vehicles. Required: High School Diploma or GED EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Kline-Life-Sports-Learning-Complex/Lifeguard_JR100557": {
      "title": "Lifeguard",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nVariable time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Athletics - Aquatics - Student Worker Administration Position Details This position performs lifeguard duties at the Kline Center Pool. Preferred Qualifications: Must be 16 years of age and have current certification in Lifeguarding, First Aid, and CPR.   Required documents: Uploaded certifications for Lifeguarding and CPR/First Aid.    Specific safety guidelines will be provided to employees, in accordance with state regulations. All individuals, including visitors, on campus are required to wear masks and follow appropriate CDC social distancing procedures at all times. Please note that employment as a Lifeguard is not able to be performed remotely. Employment and payment for hours worked will cease upon leaving campus.   Supervise all bathers/swimmers Enforce pool rules for bathers/swimmers Perform safety checks to ensure a safe facility Monitor pool water chemistry, air and water temperature Maintain current certification in Lifeguarding, First Aid and CPR Participate in in-service training for emergency procedures The pool cannot be open without appropriate and qualified staffing. This includes use by Athletic teams, Students, Faculty, Staff and Alumni Requires special skills, knowledge, or abilities. Work entails general guidelines. Moderate level of work experience or knowledge is required (minimum 6 months). Possess the knowledge and skills to perform independently with or without training. Person will have limited supervision. They will have some decision-making authority.   EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Holland-Union-Building-HUB/Serving-Area-and-Dish-Utility-Worker_JR100585": {
      "title": "Serving Area and Dish Utility Worker",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Dining Services - Dining Hall Position Details The Serving Area/Dish Utility Worker is Dining Services direct link to our student customers by interacting with students as they dine and ensuring they have a positive experience. They must maintain neat and sanitary work areas at all times, up to but not limited to all areas of the floor and dish room. They must operate the dish machine and all related equipment according to the guidelines established by the department. Essential Functions: Maintains a neat and sanitary work area at all times, by following all guidelines set by dining services HACCP program. Maintains and cleans the serving area and all related areas and equipment. Is required to be trained in all areas of the Floor and Dishroom. Maintains a safe work area and adheres to all college policies regarding safe work environments. This position is designated as “emergency response personnel”. “Emergency response personnel” are required to report to work when the college is delayed or closed. They may also be called in at any time of the day to respond to weather and/or other types of emergencies as needed. Other Functions: Must be willing to work occasional holiday dinners and seasonal picnics throughout the academic year. These events occur 2-3 times per semester. Must be able to stand up to 3 hours at a time in a buffet line and assist. Required Qualifications: Required: High School Diploma or GED. Previous customer service work in the hospitality or similar industry may substitute for a high school diploma or GED. Preferred Qualifications: ServSafe certification required or obtain certification within 1 year of hire. Physical Demands: Must be able to lift up to 30 pounds at a time. Must be able to stand, stoop, and bend the entire shift. Hours: Must be available to work days, night and weekends up to 29 hours per week EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Dining-Service---Holland-Union-Building-HUB/Casual-Caterer_JR100587": {
      "title": "Casual Caterer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nVariable time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department JM - Dining Services - Catering Position Details Dining Services supports campus food service operations. This role is ideal for individuals who enjoy working in a fast-paced environment and are committed to providing quality service to students, faculty, and staff. Job Description Assist with set up, execution, and clean-up of catered events. Essential Functions: Safe food handling practices Customer service Organizational Skills Follow Directions Serve food to event patrons Load/Unload catering trucks Work Required events/shifts as specified Bartender Specifics: Must be a minimum of 18 years old and hold a current RAMP or TIPS certification Verify identification and age requirements Prepare and responsibly serve alcoholic beverages including traditional mixed cocktails, wine bottle service and champagne service Bar set up/and tear-down/inventory and proper storage of beer, wine and liquor Marginal Functions: Occasionally work independently Proactively anticipate items needed for various functions Equipment Used: Carts, food warmers, ice machine, beverage dispensers etc. Other food service equipment, utensils, and dishes Must be 16 years old This position requires the employee to stand constantly and/or walk during the entire 4-5 hour shift, occasionally use stairs and work outdoors on an uneven surface. It also requires the employee to lift up to 50 pounds on a regular basis. Hours will vary including days, evenings and weekends. EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/50-Mooreland-Ave/Photographer---Digital-Creator_JR100584": {
      "title": "Photographer & Digital Creator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Marketing & Communication - Visual Media Position Details This is a creative position for someone with great visual instincts, stays ahead of visual and social trends, and brings a fresh and energetic perspective to the way Dickinson tells its story. Position Summary Creates vibrant, compelling visual content for the Office of Marketing and Communications, with photography serving as a central focus of the role. Captures events, portraits, campus life, branding imagery and social media content with a creative eye and strong understanding of visual storytelling. Brings awareness of current digital trends and audience engagement strategies to develop fresh, authentic content that reflects the Dickinson experience and supports the college’s communications goals. Assists with higher-level video productions, including filming, lighting, audio and other on-location production needs. Occasional evening and weekend work is required to support campus events and related assignments. Essential Functions Bring the Dickinson story to life through fresh, creative photography for the website, social media, print and digital marketing. Create dynamic, audience-focused social media content that sparks interest, encourages sharing, and strengthens brand visibility by transforming ideas into engaging digital experiences. Plan and deliver compelling photographic coverage of campus events and activities, including select evening and weekend assignments, to create, engaging visual content that enhances storytelling, builds community connections, and promotes institutional pride. Lend creative and technical experience int he development and production of high-quality video productions. Mentor and collaborate with student workers and social media ambassadors to brainstorm, test, and create content that feels authentic to the Dickinson student experience while building community. Other Duties and Responsibilities Involvement in developing messaging particularly as it involves visual content. Gear maintenance. Working with student photography positions. Other duties as determined or assigned. Supervisory Responsibilities Not responsible for supervising others. Requirements Bachelor's degree required in Photography, Digital Media, Marketing, Communications or related field. Portfolio that demonstrates previous professional photography and video production experience Portfolio should highlight ability to photograph both events and portraits, as well as professional video production. Experience with the Adobe Creative Cloud including, but not limited to Premiere, Photoshop and Lightroom. Ability to work a flexible schedule including occasional evenings and weekends. Ability for some travel. Minimum Work Experience 3-5 years Independence of Action Results are defined and existing practices are used as guidelines to determine specific work methods and carries out work activities independently; supervisor/manager is available to resolve problems. Equipment Used Sony Alpha-series mirrorless cameras. SLR lenses Lights Tripod Adobe editing software General office equipment Physical/Environmental Demands Specific physical requirements or environmental exposures Outdoor Environment: Employee work outdoors and may not be protected from weather conditions. Hazards: Includes a variety of physical conditions, such as proximity to moving mechanical parts, moving vehicles, electrical current, working on scaffolding and high places, or exposure to chemicals. EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Landis-House/Administrative-Assistant-Diversity--Equity--and-Inclusivity_JR100578": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant Diversity, Equity, and Inclusivity",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Women's and Gender Resource Center Position Details Position Summary Under the supervision of the Director of the Women’s Gender Resource Center, the Administrative Associate for Equity/Inclusivity will perform varied advanced secretarial and administrative work for the Office. This includes providing support for the Women’s and Gender Resource Center, the Popel Shaw Center for Race and Ethnicity, the Office of LGBTQ Services, and student workers. This position may have contact with high-level administrative offices and other campus departments and must be able to respond as appropriate. Essential Functions Interpret and explain established policies and procedures in response to inquiries from a variety of sources. Summarizing reports and information to facilitate review by supervisor, and investigating, evaluating and resolving problems within the scope of position. Maintains department files, record-keeping systems, and confidential materials. Provides office operations support such as receiving and screening telephone calls and visitors, scheduling meetings, conference, seminars, and special events, maintaining supervisor’s calendar. Utilizes, maintains and updates databases, software applications, and spreadsheets. Generate letters, forms, reports, mailings, requests, faxes, credit card statements, office procedures, etc. Prepares minutes, notices, manuals, agendas and correspondence with all supporting documentation, requiring application of specialized knowledge of the assigned function. Monitors and updates inventory, time, budget, payroll, and account records for office, monitors expenditures and performs simple analysis on accounts, authorizes and/or approves payments within established guidelines. Other Duties and Responsibilities Arranges necessary travel reservations and itineraries. Anticipates, and prepares background materials needed. Implements new policies, procedures, practices impacted by decisions made by directors at meetings and/or conferences. Coordinates student assistants including training, payroll, etc. departmental and student development staff. Other duties as determined or assigned. Supervision Not responsible for supervising others. Education/Requirements High school diploma or GED, required. Bachelor's degree, preferred. Additional years of directly-related office experience may substitute some education. Valid driver's license, preferred. Experience 1 to 3 years of relevant experience. Independence of Action Work progress is monitored by supervisor/manager; incumbent follows precedents and procedures, and may set priorities and organizes work within general guidelines established by supervisor/manager. Work Environment Office environment/no specific or unusual physical or environmental demands. Equipment/Tools Used Standard office equipment including computer, copier/printer, etc. Microsoft Office Suite. EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Carlisle-Pennsylvania/Communications-Officer_JR100563": {
      "title": "Communications Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Public Safety Position Details To support campus law enforcement and other public safety functions by performing activities related to processing service requests and questions; which include communications and dispatch, status monitoring, information development and communication, and records and file maintenance in a computer-aided environment. The Communications Center serves as the primary link between the public and DPS Police Officers in the field. The Communications Center is the central coordinating agency for emergency telephone calls and requests for assistance. After hours the Communications Center serves as the main information, responsible for aiding the college community and its guests with requests for service and general inquiries. Essential Functions Handles emergency and non-emergency telephone calls, prioritizes calls, and channels pertinent information to officer and supervisory personnel. Makes necessary emergency notifications. Monitors and operates police and other radio systems, fire and intrusion alarm systems, and security camera systems, and dispatches officers and other emergency personnel as needed. Monitors computer terminals for messages directed to the Department, information related to local criminal activity, and officer safety messages. Confirms warrants with responsible agencies. Provides the public with assistance on complaints and informational services, lost and found property, bicycle registration, directions, and other services. Uses tact and discretion. Observes strict confidentiality rules. Directs persons to proper supervisory level as necessary. Accurately documents officer status, location and activity. Preserves accurate logs of incoming service requests and action taken and enters, updates, and recovers information from a Computer Aided Dispatch (CAD) system. Preserves and updates various logs and records of activities, such as radio transmissions, telephone calls, tow requests, and equipment failure logs. Demonstrates knowledge of police terminology and procedures, Pennsylvania criminal and civil law as it pertains to police communications, campus geography, police services, and College policies and procedures pertaining to police communications. Provides assistance and information to persons registering vehicles at Public Safety and issues parking decals. Performs various tasks to ensure proper operation of equipment such as setting and resetting computer system, video display terminals, and printers. Assists with College fleet reservations and issues keys for reserved fleet vehicles. Required: High School Diploma or GED EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/East-College/Assistant-Professor-of-Religion_JR100572": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Religion",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Academics - Religion Position Details The Robert H. N. Ho Family Foundation Professor in Buddhist Studies at Dickinson College       The Religion Department invites applications for a tenure-track position in Buddhis t Studies with demonstrated competence in the field of Religious Studies at the rank of assistant professor beginning in Fall 2027 . We are open to candidates whose work focuses in any era, and in any geographical region (including transnational and diasporic studies of Buddhism). The successfu l candidate w ill be able to contribute to campus and department needs in one or more of the following are a s: s ustainability and development , i nterreli gious encounters, negotiations, and/or dialogue . The teaching load is five courses per year in addition to advising senior theses.   The successful candidate will hold the title of The Robert H. N. Ho Family Foundation Professor of Buddhist Studies for the first four years in the position and must have a Ph.D. in religious studies or a related field in hand by the start of appointment and demonstrate an ability to teac h in Buddhis t Studies as well as core Religious Studies courses. Further desirable qualifications include competence in other languages relevant to the study of Buddhism ( e.g. Sanskri , Pali, classical Chinese, and/or vernacular Asian language) . The Department is seeking outstanding   candidates with the potential for exceptional teaching and research. Candidates must have the ability to create learning environments that are inclusive and welcoming to all students.   Learn more about the Department at: https://www.dickinson.edu/homepage/105/religion_department   The incoming colleague will teach courses in their area of expertise in addition to the department’s core courses on rotation , including Buddhism; Buddhism and the Environment; Contemplative Practices in Asia; and Religions of Asia. In addition, they will be given support to develop at least two new courses during their pre-tenure cycle; this will include courses that incorporate the faculty’s expertise alongside key themes of sustainability, deve lopment, and global exchange. The College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, religion, age, veteran status, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or any other protected class. We encourage applications from all qualified persons.   This is a full-time, benefits-eligible position . Questions about this position should be directed to the chair of the search committee, Professor Peter Schadler schadler@dickinson.edu . Candidates should submit via Workday (online application system) at https://jobs.dickinson.edu ; please submit a cover letter , a CV , a teaching statement, a research statement, graduate transcript, names and contact information for three confidential recommenders (full recommendation letters will be sought at a later stage) . Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026, and continue until the posit ion is filled.   EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Denny-Hall/Adjunct-Faculty-in-Anthropology-Archaeology_JR100575": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty in Anthropology/Archaeology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Academics - Anthropology Job Summary/Basic Function Provide instruction using lectures, demonstrations, class discussions, and other appropriate modes of educational delivery to promote student learning in keeping with faculty academic freedom and responsibility. Foster student development and contribute to the intellectual and social life of the academic department. Maintain laboratories and equipment when applicable. Be available to faculty and students for consultation in one’s area of expertise. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Dining-Service---Holland-Union-Building-HUB/Door-Checker-Monitor_JR100570": {
      "title": "Door Checker/Monitor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Dining Services - Dining Hall Job Summary/Basic Function The primary purpose of a Door Checker is to energetically greet each guest passing through the Dining Hall doors, while processing their payment, whether it be swiping a Dickinson ID card or running a credit card. The Door Checker should make every effort to positively engage the guest with light conversation while facilitating the flow of customers through the door. Essential Functions Greet guests with a positive attitude. Collect payment from each guest via ID swipe or credit card. Ability to complete total sales sheet accurately. Ability to sit or stand in place for up to 4 hours at a time and ability to move frequently in between service cleaning windows, tables, and floors. Must be able to work up to 29 hours a week. Must be flexible in work scheduling. Evenings and weekends required. Must be willing to work several holiday dinners and seasonal outdoor picnics throughout the academic year. These events occur approximately 2- 3 per semester. Must be willing to work the buffet serving lines for these events, when needed, by standing in place near the buffet to help re-stock items for up to 3 hours at a time. Emergency Response Designation: This position is designated as \"emergency response personnel.\" \"Emergency response personnel\" are required to report to work when the college is delayed or closed. \"Emergency response personnel\" may be called in at any time of day to respond to weather and / or other types of emergencies as needed.   Preferred Qualifications: High School diploma or GED Retail operations, specifically use of a cash register and credit card machine. Customer service experience will substitute for a high school diploma or GED. Physical Demands: Must be able to sit for 4 hour periods and swipe student ID's through our access control system reader. Hours: Flexible schedule to include evenings and weekends, 3-6 hours per day, 12-29 hours per week. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Dickinson-College/Salad-Department-Worker_JR100569": {
      "title": "Salad Department Worker",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Dining Services - Kitchen Job Summary/Basic Function Salad Department workers are responsible for preparing all cold food items produced in the salad Department according to guidelines established by Dining Services, to include a variety of cooking methods and equipment. Workers are responsible for setting up appropriate sauce bars, condiment bars, pre-meal coffee brewing, and other special dining room stations for themed menus, events, and special salad bar menus. Workers are responsible for coordinating pick-up of catering orders and assembly of items for function sheets/catered events and retail locations, including the drawing of beverages, brewing coffee, and the preparation of retail crudités, yogurt parfaits, and fruit bowls/cups and salads. Essential Duties: Produces colorful eye appealing tasty daily dining hall breakfast bar, salad bar, and Grab & Go items following established par stock levels, standardized recipes. and defined procedures. Prepares specialty bar ingredients and topping or condiment bars for catered functions and dining hall events or themed meals according to the guidelines and standard recipes established by the Executive Chef or Sous Chef for Catering. Ensures safety of self, co-workers, and customers by maintaining a clean and neat, safe and sanitary work place following ServSafe procedures, HACCP guidelines, and OSHA regulations or college policies. Prepares food items for retail operations; includes parfait cups, crudité cups, to-go salads, and to-go fruit containers. Responsible for special function board items for any special production items or products necessary for catered events, assigned pick-up items, dining hall menus, events, themed meal programs, and draws beverages for “function sheet” orders; coordinates delivery of pick-up items, desserts, and salads for picnics, catered functions, etc. Assists in new product and recipe development. This position is designated as “emergency response personnel”. “Emergency response personnel” are required to report to work when the college is delayed or closed. They may also be called in at any time of the day to respond to weather and/or other types of emergencies as needed.   Other Duties May Include: Track amounts of product used at assigned station. Report amount to chef for record purposes. Monitor dates on product boxes to double check FIFO. Return copies of all cash operation orders, as they are filled to proper location for billing purposes. Required Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED with 1-3 years of relevant work experience. Preferred Qualifications: Vocational or technical certificate/degree in Culinary Arts. Serv-Safe certified or obtain certification within one year of hire. Physical Demands: This position requires the employee to stand the entire shift and lift 50 pounds on a regular basis. The position also requires bending, twisting and stooping. Work Schedule This position will work both day and evening shifts starting as early as 6:00 a.m. and working as late as 10:00 p.m. for a total of 40 hours. Days off will vary depending on business needs. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Holland-Union-Building-HUB/Cook_JR100567": {
      "title": "Cook",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Dining Services - Kitchen Job Summary/Basic Function This is a hands-on food production position. The cook must have the ability to work in all production stations in the kitchen, dining room, and service line. Duties include quality food preparation through the use of standardized recipes; assisting the chef with recipe validation by verifying quantities of ingredients used, methods used, and resulting yield; and cleaning and maintaining appliances, production utensils, and work areas. Essential functions : Produces high quality food products by using approved cooking methods and by following standardized recipes. Accurately completes production sheets for all items produced in a timely manner (same day; preferably at end of meal). Works at action stations on the line, in the dining hall, and at events as assigned and prepares food quickly, with high quality, in a pleasant and entertaining manner. Ensures safety of self and others by following best practices defined by ServSafe, HACCP steps, and OSHA and college policies and procedures. Performs pre-meal/advanced preparation and JIT production using all the following methods of food production: broil, bake, stew, braise, roast, grill, sauté, and deep fry; also slices, dices, chops, mixes, marinates, and blends. Responsible for producing assigned foods; directing servers on proper portion size and service techniques/utensils/plating of assigned foods; and ensures assigned food is garnished and presented in an attractive manner. Cooperates with and supports all other employees and departments as needed. Performs any other duties as requested by management. This position is designated as “emergency response personnel”. “Emergency response personnel” are required to report to work when the college is delayed or closed. They may also be called in at any time of the day to respond to weather and/or other types of emergencies as needed. Qualifications Required: High School Diploma or GED with 1-3 years of related experience. Preferred: Vocational or technical certificate/degree in Culinary Arts Current ServSafe certification or obtain certification within one year Physical Demands: This position requires the employee to stand for prolong periods of time. Employee must have the ability to lift 50 pounds as needed. Ability to use hands and fingers to manipulate equipment, knives and food products. Must be able to see-including color distinction, smell, and taste. Advertised Work Schedule Hours vary depending on business needs. This position will work both day and evening shifts starting as early as 5:30 a.m. and working as late as 10:00 p.m. for a total of 40 hours. Days off will vary depending on business needs. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Facilities-Management/Mechanical-Plumbing-Technician_JR100404": {
      "title": "Mechanical Plumbing Technician",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Facilities Management - Trades - Mechanical Job Summary/Basic Function Performs work on plumbing and piping systems, to include supply and drains, transporting liquids, gases, and steam. Also related fixtures, controls and metering equipment. Essential Functions: Maintains, repairs, and installs potable water systems and related equipment Maintains, repairs and installs sewage and storm water systems and related equipment Maintains and repairs sprinkler systems and related equipment Maintains, repairs and installs gas systems to include compressed air, natural gas and vacuum. works on systems that supply laboratories Monitors and maintains equipment and chemicals for treatment of pool water Keep detailed records of materials and labor time. Input data into work order system. Requirements: High school diploma or GED This position requires a  valid   driver 's license for the operation of a company owned, rented or leased vehicle. 3-5 years Work Experience Preferred: Vocational or technical certficate / degree  - Plumbing EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Facilities-Management/Mechanical-Maintenance-Technician_JR100405": {
      "title": "Mechanical Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Facilities Management - Trades - Mechanical Job Summary/Basic Function 2nd shift Maintenance Technician Maintains, services, and installs various campus mechanical systems. Essential Functions: Install, service, and repair food service equipment and maintain and service various domestic appliances (washers, dryers, ovens, refrigerators). Install, build, and repair locks, lock-sets and hardware to include automatic card access. Fabricate (welding/cutting) as needed for repairs to structural components. Service and maintain various powered housekeeping equipment Keep detailed records of materials and labor time. Input data into work order system.   Requirements: High School Diploma or GED Ability to read and write English. Ability to obtain a Forklift Operators certification.   3-5 years Work experience This position requires a  valid driver's   license   for the operation of a company owned, rented or leased vehicle. Preferred: Vocational or technical certificate/degree EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Dickinson-College/Senior-Advancement-Officer_JR100522-1": {
      "title": "Senior Advancement Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Advancement - Major & Planned Gifts Job Summary/Basic Function This senior-level gift officer engages alumni, parents, and friends to align their philanthropic interests with Dickinson’s fundraising priorities. The role focuses on building and strengthening relationships through personal outreach, identifying donor passions, developing strategies that help donors achieve their philanthropic goals. The position will solicit gifts up to 7-figures, and also steward major and planned giving donors to deepen engagement and grow support over time. In addition to major gift fundraising, and regional engagement, the role may lead or support special fundraising initiatives in donor-aligned affinity areas as approved. Significant travel is required, as is the willingness and ability to maintain strong connections to the campus community.   Position Summary Working with alumni, parents, and friends to facilitate their engagement with the college and to find a match between their philanthropic interests and Dickinson's fundraising priorities, the position expectations include meeting with these individuals in person.  The position is focused on developing relationships, learning about potential donor passions and interests, and planning steps that will allow them to fulfill their philanthropic goals with Dickinson. Also, this position works with prior major and planned giving donors to Dickinson to continue to steward them, deepen the relationship, and increase their support over time.  In addition to major gift work, this senior level gift officer position will facilitate special efforts as approved around viable affinity areas of interest to donors.   Essential Functions Solicit gifts of $100,000 or more from alumni, parents and friends. Manage the philanthropic relationship of alumni, parents, and friends who reside in assigned regions, that includes, but is not limited to, their identification, qualification, cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship. Manage a portfolio of 125-135 prospects, performing all administrative work essential to keeping information current in the database (prioritizing prospects, writing strategies, completing reports, etc.). Collaborate with colleagues on the major gift team and the broader College Advancement staff to fulfill the identified goals of the department. These activities could include, but are not limited to, staffing events, supporting other gift officers in their indentification, cultivation and solicitation of donors, and soliciting gifts for the Dickinson Fund, Other Duties and Responsibilities Collaborate with colleagues within the department and across campus. Attend staff meetings. Other duties as determined or assigned. Supervisory Responsibilities Not responsible for supervising others. Requirements Bachelor's degree required. Master's degree preferred. Valid driver's license for the operation of a company-owned, rented or leased vehicle. Demonstrated ability to build and maintain strong relationships with prospective donors through effective one-on-one engagement. Advanced verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Exceptional organizational and time management skills, with the ability to manage multiple prospects, meetings, and follow-up activities. Strong strategic thinking skills, including the ability to develop and execute donor cultivation and solicitation plans. Analytical skills to assess donor interests, giving capacity, and engagement opportunities. Ability to exercise sound judgment, discretion, and professionalism in handling sensitive and confidential information. Strong intuition and emotional intelligence, with the ability to connect genuinely with individuals and understand their motivations and interests. Self-motivated and results-oriented, with the ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with colleagues and campus partners. Ability to plan, prioritize, and follow through on action items resulting from donor meetings and engagement activities. Flexibility and willingness to travel regularly for donor visits, events, and college functions. Availability to attend and represent the College at evening and weekend events as needed. Minimum Work Experience 5-8 years Independence of Action Results are defined and existing practices are used as guidelines to determine specific work methods and carries out work activities independently; supervisor/manager is available to resolve problems. Equipment Used Standard office equipment. Physical and Environmental Demands Office environment. No specific physical demands. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Dining-Service---Holland-Union-Building-HUB/Dining-Hall-Serving-Line---Kitchen-Janitorial-Casual_JR100536": {
      "title": "Dining Hall-Serving Line & Kitchen Janitorial Casual",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nVariable time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department JM - Dining Services - Dining Hall Job Summary/Basic Function Dining Services supports campus food service operations. This role is ideal for individuals who enjoy working in a fast-paced environment and are committed to providing quality service to students, faculty, and staff. General Summary of Job Duties Odd Jobs • Taking out trash, recyclables or boxes as needed. • Check with the Chefs and Cooks as to which equipment needs to be cleaned up to and including large kettles, walls, wacks and other various equipment. • Work on any special tasks assigned by the Supervisor on Duty. • Cleaning tables, sinks, carts. • Sweeping, scrubbing and mopping of floors in the kitchen and serving areas • Cleaning of dock area. Pot Sink • Wash all pots and pans thoroughly. • Store all pots and pans upside down on appropriate shelves. • Clean all utensils brought to the pot sink and then store in appropriate areas. • Clean pot washing machine inside and out. • Clean all shelving and walls in pot sink area. • Taking out trash. • Sweep and mop floor in pot sink area. • Work on any special tasks as assigned by the Supervisor on Duty. Janitorial • Cleaning bathrooms. • Sweeping and mopping hallways and bathrooms. • Cleaning and vacuuming offices. • Sweeping and mopping floors in Dining Hall. • Sweeping and mopping Salad Department. • Taking out trash. • Cleaning refrigerator and freezer doors. • Cleaning hallway walls. • Assisting Odd Jobs or Pots as needed. • Work on any special tasks as assigned by the Supervisor on Duty. Serving • Assist in stocking, serving of food on our serving lines. • Cleaning of serving line areas. • Assisting on the grill serving line. • Making sandwiches, cutting desserts. • Any other special tasks as assigned by the Supervisor on Duty. Preferred Qualifications Physical Requirements: Must be 16 years old and some high school wanted. • Lifting up to 50 pounds • Food Handling • Prolonged Standing or Walking • Bending/Kneeling Personal Protective Equipment • Gloves • Towels for hot items • Protective eye wear when using chemical cleaners • Filter masks when using chemical cleaners EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Kline-Life-Sports-Learning-Complex/Assistant-Track---Field-Coach_JR100535": {
      "title": "Part-Time Assistant Track & Field Coach - Sprints",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nVariable time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Athletics - Track & Field Job Summary/Basic Function The Assistant Coach supports the Head Coach in all aspects of an athletic program, including but not limited to player development, the recruitment of prospective student-athletes, administration of practices, game preparation and execution, and program operations. This role assists with the planning and implementation of training sessions, provides feedback and mentorship to student-athletes, and helps develop strategies for competition. Assistant Coaches may also be responsible for specific areas such as scouting, video analysis, strength and conditioning, or skill development for particular positions or groups. Additional responsibilities often include supporting the academic progress and personal development of student-athletes, coordinating team travel and logistics, assisting with fundraising and community service initiatives, and contributing to the overall culture and success of the program. The position requires strong communication, leadership, and organizational skills, as well as a commitment to sportsmanship, inclusion, and the academic mission of the institution. Assistant Coaches are expected to work collaboratively with the Head Coach, athletic department staff, and other campus partners, and to model professionalism and integrity in all interactions. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Facilities-Management/Athletic-Field-Specialist_JR100526": {
      "title": "Athletic Field Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Facilities Management - Grounds and Landscaping Job Summary/Basic Function This position serves as the specialist responsible for the care, growth, appearance, maintenance and safety of athletic fields and athletic complex grounds. Additionally, the Athletic Field Specialist functions as a working member of College’s grounds crew (Groundskeeper I), in performing various duties to maintain and assure the attractive appearance of campus through daily execution of planned maintenance activities. Crew members are expected to maintain their individual campus zone with minimal supervision and direction. Crew members should be able to plan, prioritize and execute their activities such that the required work gets done with minimal intervention from their supervisor(s). Essential Functions Maintains natural and synthetic athletic fields and grounds to a professional level. This includes fertilization, aerification, pest and disease monitoring and treatment, turf grass establishment and overseeding, turf grass and landscape weed control, ancillary field maintenance including management of infield and warning track surfaces. Completes grooming, mowing, trimming and other turf grass maintenance activities in secondary areas of Dickinson Park and Biddle Field. Ensures work is done in a safe, professional, and productive manor. Attends seminars and safety training as required by the Director of Grounds. Maintains pesticide applicator certification via update trainings. Maintains pesticide application log. Operate, maintain and monitor automatic irrigation systems and repair as needed. Maintain and repair equipment to include mowers, sprayers, tractors, field rakes, etc. Blade sharpening. Weekly safety monitoring of all equipment. Assist with snow removal from campus sidewalks, parking lots, driveways and steps. All grounds crew members are considered “emergency response personnel.” As such they are required to report to work even when the college is closed or is operating under a delayed start. Grounds crew members can be called in at any time of day to respond to weather and/or other types of emergencies as needed. It is expected that the employee has reliable transportation adequate to transport them to work even under adverse weather conditions. Requirements Associate's Degree - Horticulture, turf grass management, agronomy. This position requires a  valid driver's   license   for the operation of a company owned, rented or leased vehicle Preferred: Bachelor's degree - Horticulture, turf grass management, agronomy. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Dickinson-College/Retail-Operations-Attendant---Barista-9-month-PT_JR100516": {
      "title": "Retail Operations Attendant - Barista 9 month PT",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Dining Services - Retail Operations Job Summary/Basic Function Provides products and services to guests as appropriate to assigned retail location. Follows proper food handling techniques and recipes, delivers excellent customer service, maintains good sanitation and cleanliness practices, and provides customers with an enjoyable experience during all meal periods. Assists with training retail new staff as needed. May be assigned to various retail operation locations on campus. Primary duties Include: Attendants are responsible for positively greeting guests, providing excellent dining experiences and service to customers, preparing quality product utilizing recipes and all necessary equipment, and ensuring unit is well stocked and organized in a neat, clean manner. POS   register Food preparation (cold and hot) Non-alcoholic drink preparation General utility duties Assist in training staff Follows   HACCP   guidelines, Pennsylvania Department of Health regulations,   OSHA   regulations, safety policies, and ServSafe standards; ensures the cleanliness of prepartation areas, all seating, and serving areas; documents   HACCP   information such as food and equipment temperatures, times of food batches, packing data for food set-ups on the line, e.g. label information for pre-packaged deli salads. Assists guests with food allergies, special requests and customized preparation, and possesses a working knowledge of food ingredients. Follows policies and procedures to ensure that all facilities and equipment are left in the appropriate condition at the end of each shift. Follows proper cash handling policies and procedures. Promotes positive relationships within and outside of the department through effective communication. This position is designated as “emergency response personnel”. “Emergency response personnel” are required to report to work when the college is delayed or closed. They may also be called in at any time of the day to respond to weather and/or other types of emergencies as needed. Other Duties May Include: Assist the Retail Operations Manager as needed. Detailed cleaning in units. Support special events and programs. Ensure a safe and inclusive environment is maintained in assigned location. Requirements: High School Diploma or   GED Experience in a food service operation preferred but not required. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Holland-Union-Building-HUB/Assistant-Director-for-Residence-Life_JR100501": {
      "title": "Assistant Director for Residence Life",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Residence Life Job Summary/Basic Function Position Summary Consistent with the college’s mission of providing a useful education for engaged citizens, the Assistant Director will play an integral role in the residential experience, developing and implementing community initiatives and overseeing an environment that supports students in the complexities of living together. The incumbent works with the fellow staff to create a vision for community development within a liberal arts setting that intentionally supports an engaging academic and intellectual environment for students beyond the classroom walls. This live-in position creates and facilitates distinctive conditions and programs throughout the residential experience that intentionally foster community, promote curiosity, and seek engagement from its members so that they are able to thrive throughout their experience. The Assistant Director reports to the Associate Director of Campus Life for Residence Life & Housing. Essential Functions Provide leadership and oversight for a four-year residential community of approximately 500–700 students by fostering an inclusive, safe, and engaging living environment that supports student success and development. Maintain a visible presence through regular student engagement, which includes but not limited to, building walkthroughs, office hours, and community initiatives. Respond to student concerns by providing support, facilitating conflict resolution, coordinating room changes, making appropriate referrals, and collaborating with campus partners. Develop and implement programming aligned with the residential curriculum to promote student learning and community engagement. Maintain accurate records, monitor residential facilities with community advisors and resident advisors to address maintenance and safety concerns, and serve as a liaison among students, faculty, staff, and families to support effective residence life and housing operations. 30% Provide direct supervision, training, and evaluation of 1–2 community advisors (head resident advisors) and 18–22 resident advisors or 8 house and apartment managers through regular individual meetings, weekly staff meetings, and oversight of residential curriculum implementation. Manage administrative processes, purchasing, and budget reconciliation to support student staff programming and approved work-related purchases while ensuring compliance with departmental and institutional policies. 20% Serve as chair for one or more Residence Life and Housing committees, including Student Staff Selection, Student Staff Training, and Programmatic Curriculum, providing leadership in the planning, implementation, and assessment of departmental initiatives. Oversee one or more departmental focus areas, such as the First-Year Experience, Upper-Class Experience, or Housing Operations by developing strategies, coordinating initiatives, and collaborating with campus partners to advance departmental goals and enhance the residential student experience. 20% Develop and maintain collaborative partnerships with campus departments, community organizations, and external stakeholders to coordinate programs and services that enhance the residential experience. Collaborate with campus partners, including Public Safety, Facilities Management, and CASE, to support the effective operation of residential facilities, oversee residential key management, and ensure timely resolution of operational needs. Support and participate in Campus Life initiatives and maintain Residence Life and Housing website content to provide accurate and timely information to students and the campus community. 10% Provide 24/7 on-call crisis response and administrative support for the residential campus by participating in a four-person professional staff on-call rotation, serving as the college's Administrator on-call, and maintaining a required 30-minute response time while on-call. Assess and respond to student emergencies and critical incidents within the residential community, implementing appropriate crisis response protocols and collaborating with campus partners to ensure the safety, well-being, and support of students and the campus community. 10% Coordinate and oversee the opening and closing of residential facilities by collaborating with student staff to prepare buildings for occupancy, including the completion and management of Room Condition Reports. Supervise closing processes to ensure spaces are inspected, damages are accurately documented and assessed, and health and safety inspections are completed prior to residence hall break closings in compliance with institutional policies and standards. 10% Other Duties and Responsibilities This position is a 12-month live-in position. Assist with Campus Life special event planning and coordination. Participate in departmental, divisional, or college committees as appointed. Participate in the student conduct resolution process by facilitating the informal resolution process and administrative hearings for assigned cases as needed. Other duties as determined or assigned. Supervisory Responsibilities Not responsible for supervising others. Requirements Bachelor’s degree in Counseling, Higher Education Administration, or related field, required. A valid driver’s license for the operation of a company-owned, rented or leased vehicle. Pennsylvania Act 153 Clearance consisting of the Pennsylvania Criminal History Record Information Check, Pennsylvania Child Abuse Certification, and Federal Criminal History Record Information Check pursuant to Pennsylvania law and Dickinson College policy. Experience in Residence Life and Housing, specifically within first-year programming, hall support, etc., is preferred, but not required. Experience working with eRezLife is preferred. Strong customer service skills to deal with situations tactfully and promptly. Flexible hours including nights and weekend commitments. Ability to routinely access student residence halls and other campus facilities, including walking throughout buildings and climbing and descending stairs in the course of performing job responsibilities, with or without a reasonable accommodation. Work Experience 1-3 years Independence of Action Results are defined and existing practices are used as guidelines to determine specific work methods and carries out work activities independently; supervisor/manager is available to resolve problems. Equipment Used Standard office equipment. Physical and Environmental Demands Ability to routinely access student residence halls and other campus facilities, including walking throughout buildings and climbing and descending stairs in the course of performing job responsibilities, with or without a reasonable accommodation. Office environment. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Waidner-Spahr-Library/Student-Technology-Support---Engagement-Specialist_JR100504": {
      "title": "Student Technology Support & Engagement Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department User Services - Computing Specialists Job Summary/Basic Function The Student Technology Support & Engagement Specialist ensures effective IT support at Dickinson College by managing the student technical staff at the Help Desk, coordinating support for student-owned technology and maintaining the campus loaner laptop program. This position also creates technical documentation, maintains the User Services Knowledge Base and collaborates with User Services and Academic Technology liaisons. Lastly, this position serves as backup for the Help Desk when needed and communicates IT resources and services to campus. The Student Technology Support & Engagement Specialist ensures effective IT support at Dickinson College. They manage recruitment, training, scheduling, and supervision of student technical staff at the Help Desk and the ResNet Services Annex student computer support location. They coordinate support for student-owned technology and the campus loaner laptop program in conjunction with student-facing support. This position also creates technical documentation for campus-supported technologies and maintains the User Services Knowledge Base, ensuring the documentation is posted and updated as required. In the application of that technical knowledge, the position collaborates with User Services and Academic Technology liaisons on IT training for faculty, students, and staff as needed, including developing training materials, conducting workshops, and providing one-on-one support. The position serves as backup for the Help Desk when needed and communicates IT resources and services to the campus. Position requires strong communication, technical troubleshooting, and organizational skills. Position works independently and collaboratively within a dynamic support environment. Essential Functions This position is responsible for recruiting, hiring, training, scheduling, and supervising the User Services student technical team to ensure they are effectively integrated into departmental operations. The role oversees the daily functions of the Student Help Desk, ResNet Services Annex, and the Hardware Support Assistant positions, ensuring consistent and high-quality service delivery. Providing regular performance feedback, coaching, and mentorship to student employees is a key responsibility, supporting their development and success. Additionally, the position maintains and updates the student staff handbook, operational policies, and support workflows to reflect evolving procedures and uphold institutional standards. The position is responsible for maintaining and expanding User Services’ internal and public-facing Knowledge Base of technical documentation. This includes writing and editing clear, accurate how-to guides and collaborating with both professional and student staff to update existing materials. The role also involves evaluating current documentation systems and developing strategies to improve accessibility, usability, and overall effectiveness for a diverse user audience. This position plans and coordinates IT training opportunities for students, faculty, and staff, including workshops, orientation events, and drop-in support sessions. It involves partnering with departments, administrative offices, Computing Specialists, and Academic Technology to assess training needs and develop targeted instructional materials, with an emphasis on making relevant content available through the Knowledge Base. The role also represents User Services in campus initiatives and collaborates on technology onboarding activities related to the academic calendar. The role includes creating and distributing student-focused IT communications through email and other platforms, ensuring messages are clear, informative, and timely. It involves developing and implementing strategies to engage students through digital channels, with consideration for the effective use of social media where appropriate. Additionally, the position ensures the accurate and prompt dissemination of information related to service outages, system updates, and available technology resources. This position oversees the health, readiness, and imaging of the college’s loaner laptop fleets, ensuring that devices are properly maintained and fully functional. It includes coordinating with Help Desk staff to support efficient and consistent laptop checkout and check-in procedures. The role also involves maintaining system updates, performing diagnostics, and addressing technical issues as needed to keep the fleet in optimal working condition. The position serves as the designated backup to the full-time Help Desk Specialist, providing front-line user support during absences, high-demand periods, or other critical times. It also includes assisting with the mentoring of student staff by guiding them through escalated support issues and reinforcing Help Desk procedures to ensure consistent and effective service. Requirements Associate's Degree - Information Technology or a related field. 1-3 Years work experience Preferred Bachelor's Degree - Information Technology, Computer Science, Education, or a related discipline. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/50-Mooreland-Ave/Donor-Engagement-Officer-Senior-Donor-Engagement-Officer_JR100500": {
      "title": "Donor Engagement Officer/Senior Donor Engagement Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Advancement - Donor Engagement Job Summary/Basic Function Position Summary The Donor Engagement Officer (DEO) is a highly organized and self-driven member of the Donor Engagement (DE) team within the Division of College Advancement, which oversees Dickinson’s fundraising and alumni and parent engagement programs. Reporting to the Director of Donor Engagement, this position serves as a key partner to the Principal and Individual Giving teams, managing and executing meaningful curated engagement experiences for Dickinson’s highest rated donors that are both rewarding for the donor and beneficial to the college. The DEO serves as the project manager for all identified strategic donor engagement opportunities – both on campus and virtual– coordinating logistics, partnering with faculty and staff across campus, ensuring consistent communication and exceptional execution from concept to completion. The DEO is primarily responsible for coordinating 40-60 high impact engagement (HIE) programs for donors. The DEO also collaborates with the donor engagement team to execute the work of this office including cultivation and stewardship activities like proposal development, gift impact reporting, individualized stewardship plans, special events, donor recognition programs, and other duties as assigned. The DEO partners with multiple campus offices including the Office of the President, academic affairs, global studies, campus life, athletics and external vendors who support Dickinson’s donor engagement program. This position involves regular engagement with Dickinson’s major donors, trustees, faculty, students, staff, and the college’s community of alumni, parents, and friends. Evidence of strong project management skills is essential. The successful candidate will also possess exceptional relationship-building abilities and the initiative to collaborate across campus to identify engagement opportunities aligned with donor interest. This individual will become deeply knowledgeable about campus programs and serve as a trusted resource to the Individual Giving team, helping translate fundraising strategies into meaningful donor experiences. Essential Functions High Impact Engagement: Serve as project manager to plan and execute high impact engagement programs in collaboration with relationship managers and campus partners with a focus on customized campus visits and virtual visits for top donors and prospects. Manage all tasks related to the creation and execution of multiple finely detailed programs simultaneously (approximately 5-10 programs at any one time) while ensuring exceptional attention to detail. Develop project timelines, coordinate internal stakeholders, manage logistics, pre-program preparation and day-of execution, monitor expenses, and oversee post-engagement assessment. This involves working regularly with major gift fundraisers and colleagues throughout the Division of College Advancement and across campus. Maintain standards of excellence in donor service while ensuring a seamless experience for all participants. Principal Gift and Major Gift Donor Strategies: Support work of the individual giving team by becoming deeply knowledgeable about campus activities. Develop and maintain strong relationships with faculty, administrators, and staff across campus and build a comprehensive understanding of college priorities, academic programs, student initiatives, faculty expertise, and institutional activities. Attend campus events, presentations, and programs to remain informed about current initiatives and engagement opportunities. Identify and cultivate a network of campus contacts who can support donor engagement efforts. Donor Recognition Society Engagement and Special Events: The DEO supports special events and communications to engage and recognize donors who are members of the college’s giving societies, namely John Dickinson Society, Mermaid Society, Old West Society and Founders’ Society. Proposal Development and Impact Reporting: Work with the DE team, divisional and campus partners annually to create approximately personalized donor endowment and current use gift impact reports using an online report platform. Support senior team leaders in the development of fundraising proposals for principal and major gift donors. This includes collaboration with cross-campus partners and consultants. Project Management and Operational Excellence: Develop and implement processes and procedures that improve efficiency, consistency, and effectiveness. Utilize project management tools and systems to monitor progress and manage deliverables. Maintain timelines, communications, and project documentation. Other Duties and Responsibilities Expectation to staff major all-college event weekends such as Homecoming and Family Weekend, Commencement, and Alumni Weekend. Other duties as determined or assigned. Supervisory Responsibilities Not responsible for supervising others Requirements Bachelor's degree Valid driver's license for the operation of a company-owned, rented or leased vehicle. Minimum Work Experience 1-3 years (Donor Engagement Officer) 5 - 8 years (Senior Donor Engagement Officer) Independence of Action Results are defined; incumbent sets own goals and determines how to accomplish results with few or no guidelines to follow, although precedents may exist; supervisor/manager provides broad guidance and overall direction. Physical/Environmental Demands Office environment No specific or unusual physical demands. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Kaufman-Hall/Adjunct-Instructor-of-Psychology-1_JR100494": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Psychology-1",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Academics - Psychology Job Summary/Basic Function Adjunct faculty for 1 or more sections in Psychology Adjunct faculty are responsible for the synchronous teaching of one or more undergraduate courses in psychology. Successful candidates will demonstrate enthusiasm for teaching, strong commitment to undergraduate education in a liberal arts environment, and possess the ability to create inclusive learning experiences for an increasingly diverse student body. Psychology courses typically enroll up to 35 students. Responsibilities include preparing course materials, delivering instruction, assessing student performance, maintaining accurate course records, and adhering to departmental and college policies. Adjunct faculty are expected to hold regular office hours to support students, respond to student inquiries in a timely manner, and provide academic guidance related to course content. Qualifications include a master's degree (completed or in progress) in psychology or a closely related field (doctoral degree preferred) and demonstrated ability to teach effectively at the undergraduate level. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Carlisle-Pennsylvania/Assistant-Baseball-Coach_JR100485": {
      "title": "Assistant Baseball Coach",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Athletics - Baseball Job Summary/Basic Function Pitching Coach Position Summary Responsible for aiding the Head Baseball Coach in all aspects of a Dickinson Baseball program, including but not limited to the recruitment of prospective student-athletes, administration of practices, marketing and implementation of clinics, leadership development and game strategy. Essential Functions Team Management and Player Development: Oversee the management and mentoring of the men's baseball team, and specifically the pitching staff, by fostering a culture of accountability, discipline, and a strong team mentality. Assist with the strength and conditioning program for the baseball team. Reinforce the head coach's expectations for player behavior, commitment, and standards of performance both on and off the field. Help players develop their mental and mechanical skills while cultivating a positive, competitive team environment. 25% Recruitment and Athlete Relations: Play a pivotal role in recruiting talented baseball student athletes to the program through scouting, evaluation, and communication with prospective student-athletes and their families. Manage the recruiting database (e.g., Front Rush/Slate) and clearly communicate the values and culture of the college and the baseball program during the recruiting process. Establish a strong pipeline of future student-athletes who align with the program's mission. 25% Practice and Game Preparation: Assist the head coach in planning and coordinating daily team practices, ensuring that training sessions are purposeful and focused on developing both individual skills and team strategy. Must be able to throw batting practice and hit fungos. Contribute to game days through the scouting of opponents, and provide input into game plans and lineup decisions. Help analyze game film, create video analysis, and offer coaching feedback to improve team performance. 25% Logistics and Team Operations: Coordinate all travel logistics for the baseball team, including organizing transportation, accommodations, and meal planning for away games and tournaments. Support the team’s fundraising efforts and facilitate team events that promote community engagement and program growth. Assist with marketing and promotional activities, including managing communication with alumni, recruits, and the broader baseball community through social media, emails, and other. 15% Field Prep: Coordinate with grounds grew to assist in field game prep. 10% Other Duties and Responsibilities Other duties as determined or assigned. Supervision Guides work of others who perform essentially the same work. May organize, set priorities, schedule and review work, but has no responsibility to hire, terminate, review performance or make pay decisions. Education/Requirements Bachelor's degree, required. Master's degree, preferred. This position is subject to the Pennsylvania Act 153 Clearance consisting of the Pennsylvania Criminal History Record Information Check, Pennsylvania Child Abuse Certification, and Federal Criminal History Record Information Check pursuant to Pennsylvania law and Dickinson College policy. Valid driver's license. Experience 1 to 3 years of relevant experience. Independence of Action Work progress is monitored by supervisor/manager; incumbent follows precedents and procedures, and may set priorities and organizes work within general guidelines established by supervisor/manager. Work Environment Office environment. Specific physical requirements or environmental exposures: Outdoor Environment: Employees work outdoors and may not be protected from weather conditions. Equipment/Tools Used Standard office equipment. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Waidner-Admissions-House/Assistant-Director-of-Admissions_JR100438": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Admissions",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Admissions - Greater Capital Job Summary/Basic Function The Assistant Director of Admissions serves as an experienced admissions professional whose responsibilities include the administration of a recruitment territory from inquiry to enrollment, serving as a member of the core recruitment team, and evaluating applications and documentation. This type of territory management requires leadership, independent thinking, strategic planning, and some budget management. In addition, this position will support the broader work of the enrollment division and its ongoing initiatives and goals by managing essential projects, representing the college virtually, on-campus, and off-campus, collaborating actively with office throughout the college, and seeking out leadership opportunities through regional and national organizations. Essential Functions: Manage a recruitment territory by aligning a strategy plan with divisional goals in collaboration with this position’s supervisor, establishing and hitting benchmarks and goals, cultivating and maintaining relationships with prospective students, parents, counselors, independent educational consultants, and alumni/parent volunteers. Represent the college by conducting/attending on-campus, off-campus, or virtual: interviews, information sessions, presentations, forums, receptions, open houses, school visits, and college fairs. Be prepared to travel domestically and/or internationally on behalf of the college 6-8 weeks in the fall and 2-3 weeks in the spring, including nights and weekends. Evaluate admissions files by completing and reviewing candidate applications, making admissions and scholarship recommendations to the committee, and serving on the admissions selection committee. Manage at least two enrollment projects that serve to advance the core mission of the division (ex. student volunteers, programming, and outside partner management). Serve as a key member of at least one internal committee (ex. transfer admissions, athletic recruitment, admissions volunteer network, communications). Hold and seek out leadership roles in regional and national associations for college admissions counseling and other regional admissions associations. Represent the college by taking part in presentations and group travel through these organizations. Other Duties and Responsibilities Demonstrate cultural sensitivity and be responsive to the needs of diverse constituencies. Employ excellent interpersonal, organizational, communication, negotiation, and consensus-building skills. Clearly communicate objectives, challenges, and opportunities in thoughtful, concise narratives. Maintain confidentiality, particularly as it pertains to personally identifiable information. Work well independently and as a member of a team, initiate tasks and projects, and have the capacity to manage multiple responsibilities concurrently. Show institutional-level thinking that demonstrates an understanding of Dickinson's mission. Other duties as determined or assigned. Supervisory Responsibilities Supervises work of others, including planning, assigning and scheduling work, reviewing work and ensuring quality standards, training staff and overseeing their productivity. May offer recommendations for hiring, termination and pay adjustments, but does not have responsibility for making these decisions. Requirements Bachelor's degree Valid driver's license for the operation of a company-owned, rented or leased vehicle. This position is subject to the Pennsylvania Act 153 Clearance consisting of the Pennsylvania Criminal History Record Information Check, Pennsylvania Child Abuse Certification, and Federal Criminal History Record Information Check pursuant to Pennsylvania law and Dickinson College policy. Minimum Work Experience 1-3 years Independence of Action Results are defined and existing practices are used as guidelines to determine specific work methods and carries out work activities independently; supervisor/manager is available to resolve problems. Equipment Used General office equipment. Physical/Environmental Demands Office environment. No specific or unusual physical demands. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Dining-Service---Holland-Union-Building-HUB/Catering-Supervisor_JR100458": {
      "title": "Catering Supervisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Dining Services - Catering Job Summary/Basic Function The catering supervisor assists the Catering Manager and other catering supervisors in the execution of all special functions and delivery services throughout Dining Services. Essential Functions The Catering Supervisor will oversee all phases of banquet operations. Must be enthusiastic, possess excellent communication, organizational, and time management skills, and have the ability to lead and direct a large banquet staff. Plan equipment needs and timelines for a variety of catered events. Make lists and delegate responsibilities to catering staff, or work independently to promptly set up, service, and clean up events in various locations on and off campus. Hold pre-event meetings to ensure clear expectations and instructions are given to all scheduled staff. Determine the ideal time to serve food to ensure the highest quality of service to the customer. Communicate with kitchen staff and the POC of the event as needed. Initiate and organize clean-up at the close of each function in order to utilize time as efficiently as possible. Separate items by department to ensure that the unloading and return of dishes and  equipment to proper areas is swift and timely. Plan for and occasionally lead weekly planning meetings and quarterly all catering staff meetings. Scheduling of casual catering staff via Microsoft Teams. I nventory and maintain catering equipment, linens, and disposables. Schedule and coordinate rental   equipment when necessary. Ensure all catering staff adhere to Dickinson Dining Services highest standards of food safety and alcohol safety. Prioritized the guest experience while also protecting and supporting our dedicated  staff. Other Duties Yearly inventory. Catering linen maintenance and storage. Support of other areas of Dining Services as needed Other duties as determined or assigned Supervisory Duties Supervises work of others, including planning, assigning, and scheduling work, reviewing work, and ensuring quality standards, training staff and overseeing their productivity. May offer recommendations for hiring, termination and pay adjustments, but does not have responsibility for making these decisions. Additional Requirements Valid Driver's license w/clean driving record. Serv-Safe certification or obtain certification upon hire. TIPS/RAMP trained or certify upon hire. This position is subject to the Pennsylvania Act 153 Clearance consisting of the Pennsylvania Criminal History Record Information Check, Pennsylvania Child Abuse Certification, and Federal Criminal History Record Information Check pursuant to Pennsylvania law and Dickinson College policy. Physical Demands Continual listening, hearing, talking, standing, crouching, lifting up to 50 pounds, walking, bending, stooping, climbing stairs, kneeling, squatting, balancing, pulling and pushing. This position requires you to reach overhead often. This position requires the employee to work outdoors at times and may work in extreme heat.   EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Kline-Fitness-Center/Lifeguard_JR100372-1": {
      "title": "Lifeguard",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-02\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nVariable time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Athletics - Aquatics Job Summary/Basic Function The position performs lifeguard duties at the Kline Center Pool. Must be 16 years of age and have current certification in Lifeguard Training, First Aid and CPR. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
