    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Waidner-Admissions-House/Admissions-Associate_JR100350-1": {
      "title": "Admissions Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Admissions - Northeast Job Summary/Basic Function The Admissions Associate position is a full‑time, one‑year appointment running from July 1, 2026 - June 30, 2027. The role functions as an essential member of the admissions office responsible for engaging prospective students, families and counselors through all stages of the admissions cycle. Responsibilities: Manage an assigned recruitment territory Plan and execute 6-8 weeks of recruitment travel in the fall and 2-3 weeks in the spring, including some nights and weekends. Engage prospective and accepted students through on‑campus, off‑campus, and virtual programming, including some nights and weekends Co‑lead and/or support admissions projects. Conduct personal outreach and follow-up on a consistent basis with prospective and accepted students Evaluate applications and provide recommendations to the admissions committee. Conduct interviews, information sessions, presentations, and workshops that advance the college’s outreach and enrollment goals. Perform other duties as assigned to support the needs of the admissions team. Priority consideration will be given to applicants who apply before June 1, 2026. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/Holland-Union-Building-HUB/Retail-Operations-Attendant---Juice-Barista_JR100165": {
      "title": "Retail Operations Attendant - Juice Barista",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-02-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosting Details Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Dining Services - Retail Operations Job Summary/Basic Function Provides products and services to guests as appropriate to assigned retail location. Follows proper food handling techniques and recipes, delivers excellent customer service, maintains good sanitation and cleanliness practices, and provides customers with an enjoyable experience during all meal periods. Assists with training retail new staff as needed. Essential Functions Attendants are responsible for positively greeting guests, providing excellent dining experiences and service to customers, preparing quality product utilizing recipes and all necessary equipment, and ensuring unit is well stocked and organized in a neat, clean manner. Follows HACCP guidelines, Pennsylvania Department of Health regulations, OSHA regulations, safety policies, and ServSafe standards; ensures the cleanliness of preparation areas, all seating, and serving areas; documents HACCP information such as food and equipment temperatures, times of food batches, packing data for food set-ups on the line, e.g. label information for pre-packaged deli salads. Assists guests with food allergies, special requests and customized preparation, and possesses a working knowledge of food ingredients. Follows policies and procedures to ensure that all facilities and equipment are left in the appropriate condition at the end of each shift. Follows proper cash handling policies and procedures. Promotes positive relationships within and outside of the department through effective communication.   Other Duties and Responsibilities Emergency Response Designation: This position is designated as \"emergency response personnel.\" \"Emergency response personnel\" are required to report to work when the college is delayed or closed. \"Emergency response personnel\" may be called in at any time of day to respond to weather and / or other types of emergencies as needed. ServSafe certified or obtain certification within one year of hire. Physical Demands Continuous standing and walking, often kneels, squats, bending and climbing stairs. Often lifts up to 10 pounds Communicate by hearing, listening and speaking   Scheduled Hours Monday - Friday 7 a.m. 2 p.m. during academic period. Summer work in the Dining Hall during summer camps. EEO/Diversity Statement:     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    },
    "https://dickinson.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/Jobs/job/South-College-WEST-Fin-Aid/Temporary-Financial-Aid-Specialist_JR100589": {
      "title": "Temporary Financial Aid Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAbout Dickinson Dickinson College is a premier four-year residential liberal arts institution chartered in 1783 and widely recognized as a leader in global and sustainability education. Dickinson College is located in Carlisle, named a “most livable city” by Forbes and is minutes from the state capital of Harrisburg. The campus is connected to a vibrant downtown that offers eclectic dining, shopping and entertainment options. Within a two-hour drive are Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington, D.C.; New York City is three hours away. Dickinson College offers full-time employees a broad range of benefits, including a comprehensive medical insurance plan, life insurance, flexible spending accounts, generous time off, parental leave, homebuyer assistance, and tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependent children under the age of 24. Upon eligibility, the College contributes 8% of an employee’s base salary to a retirement account with an additional .5% matching contribution; all money paid by the college into the employee’s retirement plan is immediately and fully vested in the employee. Below you will find the details for the position, including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the \"Apply\" for this job link button above. Position Department Financial Aid Position Details This is a temporary, full-time position for a one-year term, with a possibility of extension. Summary The Financial Aid Specialist will be responsible for reviewing institutional and federal financial aid applications, determining financial aid eligibility, and creating financial aid offers, using Dickinson’s financial aid system, PowerFAIDS. This person will be responsible for Senior Associate and Director level work. Serves as a professional resource for staff/system given knowledge and expertise in PowerFAIDS. May conduct Q/A sessions as learn new system. Based on past experience, may contribute insights to practices and new system. This role also entails supporting the Loan Specialist with Federal Direct Loan and private/alternative loan certification. This individual will ensure compliance with federal, state, and institutional financial aid policies. Essential Functions Review financial aid applications, resolve conflicting information, and package prospective and returning student financial aid to ensure affordability while meeting the college's enrollment, retention, and financial goals. Verify student eligibility for institutional, federal, and state financial aid by reconciliation of differences between the Free Application for Federal Student Aid and CSS profile and confirming eligibility after thorough verification of documents including parent and student tax return, W-2 forms and other required verification worksheets. Ensure compliance with federal, state, and institutional policies, and participation in training opportunities and webinars to stay current on regulation changes. Review and process Federal Direct Loan and private/alternative loan application as needed. Other Duties and Responsibilities Resolve over awards. Meet virtually with students regarding financial aid questions. Assist in clean up reports. Other duties as determined or assigned. Supervisory Responsibilities Not responsible for supervising others. Requirements Associate's degree, required. Bachelor's degree, preferred Prior experience with financial aid packaging in PowerFAIDS Demonstrated knowledge of financial aid application process Prior experience with College's Board CSS Profile and institutional methodology Ability to comply with all federal, state, and institutional policies Ability to work independently, take initiative, and follow through on tasks with minimal supervision Strong written and verbal communication skills, organization and time-management skills Ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines, professional judgement, discretion, and a collaborative approach to working across departments, strong partnerships, with a service orientation and genuine interest in institutional mission Work Experience 3-5 years Independence of Action Results are defined and existing practices are used as guidelines to determine specific work methods and carries out work activities independently; supervisor/manager is available to resolve problems. Equipment Used Standard office equipment Physical/Environmental Demands Office environment No specific or unusual physical demands EEO/Diversity Statement     The College is committed to building a representative and diverse faculty, staff, and student body. We encourage applications from all qualified persons."
    }
